Oh yeah, definitely rushing it.  When you first start the mines stay
near the stairs so you can retreat when you get in trouble.  Keep
going back into the mines until you clear the first level.  If it
takes many cycles of moving up and healing, then that's what it takes.
I go about one level deeper in the main dungeon than the mines and I
cycle back and forth until I've hit mines end on one branch and
Sokoban on the other before going deeper in the main dungeon.

Each time I get in trouble in the mines I retreat to the less crowded
main dungeon.  Each time I get hungry in the main dungeon I advance
into the crowded mines, but I usually return to the mines at full
hitpoints before getting hungry.  The crowds in the mines let me
advance quickly, the less crowded main dungeon gives my a chance to
use those newfound experience levels.

The variation for me is whether I go through minetown first or Sokoban
first, but I've usually done both before doing the rest of the mines,
and I do all of the mines and Sokoban before going deeper in the main
dungeon.

For me, by the time I've completed mines end and returned up I'm
several experience levels higher and I can handle plenty in the main
dungeon.  Also completing the mines gives plenty of good equipment and
a large stash of mediocre equipment.

